slots as slot wrappers; the value and the type it was found on."] [129 1 "// The type attribute cache (PY6-core, queue 200, after PY8's measurement: lookupAttr was 31-35% of a run;"] [130 1 "// CPython's method cache over tp_version_tag): each type keeps its lookups' answers by name, the absent ones"] [131 1 "// too, and drops them all when typeEpoch moves. typeEpoch moves on any change to a type's namespace (the dicts"] [132 1 "// marked ofType: an insertion, a replaced value, a deletion, a clear, popitem), on a getset added, and on an"] [133 1 "// MRO set (c3MRO's and readyTypes'), so an answer is never older than the namespaces it was read from."] [141 1 "// lookupAttrMRO is _PyType_Lookup's walk: t's MRO's dicts, then the getsets and slot wrappers of each."] [162 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [191 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [192 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [198 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [199 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [211 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [212 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [213 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [214 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [219 1 "// ExtTypeAttrSet, when set, is told a special attribute of a type that is not a class statement's was set or deleted"] [220 1 "// (arbace/pyctypes, a C type's: queue 594); true when it changed the type's slots."] [223 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [228 15 "// OrderedDict's tp_dictoffset (py-mods-1122)"] [255 18 "// queue 304: a property subclass's instance"] [262 38 "// _io's objects (iobase's tp_dictoffset; queue 545)"] [271 1 "// InstanceDictHook is the __dict__ of an object of another package (arbace/pyctypes' C-born objects whose type has a"] [272 1 "// tp_dictoffset: the dict their memory holds; queue 268), nil when it has none."] [275 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [276 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [277 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [278 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [279 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [285 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [286 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [288 2 "// class: the entry answers the load of the attribute from the class tp itself (queue 305, CPython's LOAD_ATTR_CLASS):"] [289 2 "// tp's metatype is type, d was found on a class statement's class of tp's MRO, and type has no data descriptor of"] [290 2 "// the name, so type.__getattribute__ answers d bound by its __get__ (None, tp), or d"] [294 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [300 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [301 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [306 1 "// attrSites are every code's inline caches (queue 241), swept by gc.collect: an entry whose epoch is past holds a type"] [307 1 "// and the value found, which CPython's caches (a version tag) do not keep alive (WeakMethod's test_method_dead: the"] [308 1 "// method deleted from its class stays in the site that loaded it). attrSwept is the epoch of the last sweep."] [314 1 "// sweepAttrSites clears the stale entries of every inline cache, once per type epoch."] [334 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [342 3 "// made at the instruction's first lookup (queue 305: a site, 192 bytes, for every instruction of a code that"] [343 3 "// ran one attribute instruction was a quarter of a program's heap, each Go collection's to mark)"] [363 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [368 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [369 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [381 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [397 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [419 1 "// typeAttrAt is load-attr of name from the class t (its metatype type) at c's instruction pc: typeGetAttr, its answer"] [420 1 "// kept in the instruction's cache entry for t when it is a class statement's attribute that type's own data"] [421 1 "// descriptors do not shadow (queue 305: deltablue's and pprint's class attributes, typeGetAttr 4-8% of their runs; the"] [422 1 "// entry is valid while typeEpoch holds, as every entry of the cache)."] [434 2 "// the entry may have moved while typeGetAttr ran Python code (a __get__): kept only when it still holds t's answer"] [443 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [444 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [453 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [456 5 "// store_instance_attr's MODIFIED, the value the same or not (queue 274)"] [466 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [469 20 "// the room of the class's next instances' dicts (newDictSized)"] [476 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [483 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [501 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [508 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [536 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [537 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [547 3 "// _PyType_Lookup of t's MRO assigns the version tag a watched modification clears (queue 274); the"] [548 3 "// metatype's data descriptors (__name__, __dict__) answer before it"] [555 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [563 4 "// a built-in type's class and static methods know their type for __qualname__"] [586 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [597 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare), a frozen class's"] [598 3 "// name (queue 270b: PyType_Freeze)"] [617 26 "// a C type's slots are its own (queue 270b: its dict changes alone)"] [619 3 "// a C type's slot the extension changed (queue 594: update_slot's __call__ over vectorcall): its subclasses'"] [620 3 "// slots refilled"] [626 19 "// type_setattro's PyType_Modified: the type watchers (queue 274)"] [631 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [639 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [642 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [645 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [654 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [666 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [667 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [668 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [675 4 "// wrapperdescr_call's check (bpo-37619: a wrapper of the wrong class in a class's dict)"] [681 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [682 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [683 4 "// queue 207)"] [687 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [688 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [744 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [765 2 "// object's attributes"] [767 2 "// a built-in type with a dictionary shows it itself (BaseException's, function's, module's); a class's is"] [768 2 "// subtype_getsets_full's, in the dict of the class that adds it (addLayoutDescrs): object has none"] [776 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [835 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[76 32] [80 32] [119 31] [146 31] [150 28] [154 35] [166 6] [166 20] [172 9] [172 23] [175 31] [179 28] [183 35] [194 26] [205 33] [326 24] [349 23] [371 18] [396 27] [404 41] [427 34] [436 50] [452 27] [454 21] [462 32] [465 34] [468 37] [489 28] [512 34] [551 33] [552 27] [566 34] [570 34] [575 34] [592 35] [613 38] [633 32] [695 33] [716 18] [752 26] [818 58]]} (go/file "attr.go" :imports [

